# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale it
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as [00:00, 06:00).
# Sources: Vocabolario Treccani
# (https://www.treccani.it/vocabolario/pomeriggio/), which gives
# pomeriggio as "la parte del giorno compresa tra il mezzodi e il
# tramonto del sole".
# The notte is the small hours of the named day. "domani notte" is
# therefore tomorrow 00:00-06:00: the sera holds the hours to midnight,
# so the notte has nowhere else to be, and re-cutting it to English's
# wrapping night would contradict the chart it comes from.
notte
